doc:    "Found by soaking the `roundtrip` oracle for 150 seconds after the const-list fix, mutating cli/tests/formatting/if_an_else_chain_breaks_together/expected.buri, and minimised to the 39 bytes here: a blank line written directly under an opening brace. `blank` never writes a line under a `{` — a gap between a brace and what is inside it is not a paragraph break somebody typed — but `Doc::Blank` is a hard break, and a hard break forces the group around it. So the first pass laid the block out broken for a reason it did not print, the next read of the file saw no blank line and laid the same block out flat, and `format` rewrote the file on every other run forever. `if (n == 0) {` / blank / `y } else {}` came back as `if (n == 0) { y } else {  }`. Pre-existing: it reproduces on the same seed against the formatter as it stood before this wave, and it is nothing to do with comments — the same class as every other finding here, which is a break in the layout that the output does not carry the cause of. Fixed in `Build::block_lines`, which now drops the gap above the *first* line of a block rather than recording a break that will print as nothing. A comment there is unaffected: it prints, so the break it forces is one the next read makes too. The printed shape is pinned by cli/tests/formatting/blank_under_an_opening_brace_is_not_a_break/. No existing formatting golden moved."
oracle: "roundtrip"
status: FIXED
